---
import Dropdown from "../components/Dropdown.astro";
import Schedule from "../components/Schedule.astro";
import ScheduleLegend from "../components/ScheduleLegend.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DropdownGroup from "../components/DropdownGroup.astro";
import KeyPoints from "../components/KeyPoints.astro";
import Sponsors from "../components/Sponsors.astro";
import Sponsor from "../components/Sponsor.astro";
import { fridaySchedule, saturdaySchedule, sundaySchedule } from "../content/events";
---

<BaseLayout
	pageTitle="Home"
	navbar={{
		leftItems: [
			{ name: "Schedule", href: "#schedule" },
			{ name: "Sponsors", href: "#sponsors" },
			{ name: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
		],
	}}
	header={{ title: "AUHack 2026", subtitle: "March 13th - 15th" }}
>
	<Section class="center" color="orange" id="signup">
		<strong class="text-lg">Sign-ups for this year's AUHack have closed.</strong>
	</Section>
	<Section color="white" id="sponsors">
		<SectionHeader align="center">Sponsors</SectionHeader>

		<Sponsors>
			<Sponsor slot="diamond" href="https://incommodities.com/" img="incommodities.png" name="InCommodities" />
			<Sponsor slot="gold" href="https://www.knowit.dk/" img="knowit.svg" name="Knowit" />
			<Sponsor slot="gold" href="https://www.prosa.dk/" img="prosa_logo.svg" name="Prosa" />
			<Sponsor slot="silver" href="https://www.beumergroup.com/" img="beumergroup.jpg" name="Beumer Group" />
			<Sponsor slot="silver" href="https://www.ida.dk/" img="ida_logo.png" name="IDA" />
			<Sponsor slot="silver" href="https://www.mjolner.dk/" img="mjolner_logo.svg" name="Mjolner" />
		</Sponsors>
	</Section>
	<Section color="blue" id="about">
		<SectionHeader>What is AUHack?</SectionHeader>

		<p>
			AUHack is one of Denmark's largest hackathons for students. Over a 36-hour period from March 13th to 15th,
			students interested in IT will meet, form groups and work intensively to create awesome prototypes and
			concepts. Whether you like to concept develop, design or code, or if you're just into IT - this is for you.
		</p>

		<p>
			Ideate, build, play, hack, share, learn and have fun! The goal for the weekend is to come up with new ideas,
			play with technology and make cool stuff. It is not about creating finished products, but an opportunity to
			share your ideas with different people, build inspiring hacks, learn from our mentors and just have fun.
		</p>

		<p>
			Our goal with the hackathon is to bring creative minds and different skill sets together. We want to see you
			form new ideas and to see what having fun and playing with technology results in through your presentations
			and demos at the end of the hackathon. So if you feel up for the challenge and are interested in IT, bring
			your skill set to the event and put it in play working on something cool.
		</p>

		<KeyPoints />
	</Section>
	<Section color="white" id="schedule">
		<SectionHeader>
			Schedule
			<ScheduleLegend slot="subtitle" class="justify-end mt-0.5" />
		</SectionHeader>
		<Schedule headline="Friday" date={new Date(2026, 2, 15)} items={fridaySchedule} />
		<Schedule headline="Saturday" date={new Date(2026, 2, 14)} items={saturdaySchedule} />
		<Schedule headline="Sunday" date={new Date(2026, 2, 15)} items={sundaySchedule} />
	</Section>
	<Section color="orange" reverse id="faq">
		<SectionHeader>FAQ</SectionHeader>

		<DropdownGroup title="General">
			<Dropdown title="I cannot code. Can I attend anyway?">
				<p>
					Sure, you should definitely attend! Whether you have written lots of code or just have a creative
					soul, this hackathon needs you! In true hackathon spirit all students are very friendly and willing
					to help each other out.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="Seriously, is it free?!">
				<p>
					Yes, we're not kidding you. Thanks to our sponsors we will provide free food, swag, snacks and
					drinks at the hackathon. Plus, there will be mentors, workshops and judges only for the sake of YOU.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="What can I win?">
				<p>
					You have the fantastic opportunity to learn new stuff, try out your skills and make new friends.
					Isn't that just great? Everyone will be a winner!... Okay, we will also have some awesome prizes.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>
		</DropdownGroup>

		<DropdownGroup title="Hacking!">
			<Dropdown title="Can I build on my hack before the event?">
				<p>
					No. That's not fair. You can come up with ideas, but not build them. You are of course allowed to
					use libraries, frameworks and templates for your hacks.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="What do people usually build?">
				<p>
					AUHack has been home to a wide variety of projects, from amazing hardware projects to the coolest VR
					Games and the most useful services and apps.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="What hardware will be available to hack on?">
				<p>
					We always have a wide spectrum of hardware available, provided by the different labs at Aarhus
					University, as well as by our sponsors. A detailed list will be available as we get closer to the
					event!
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="How do I get the hardware?">
				<p>
					We have the pleasure of being able to use all of the hardware from <a
						href="https://www.chomskylab.dk/"
						target="_blank">chomskylab.dk</a
					>!<br />
					The way this works is:<br />
					1. You make an account on the website (in the "AU-ID" field put EXTXXXXXX where the Xs are random numbers
					if you are not from here)<br />
					2. Browse the website and find the hardware that you want to use<br />
					3. Go to the nice LabTools people near the info stand and tell them the hardware that you would like to
					use<br />
					4. Wait a bit while they go and get the hardware, and<br />
					5. Use the hardware for your awesome hack!<br /><br />
					You will most likely also need some wires and such - just ask for those as well. When hacking ends you
					will have to take everything apart again and return it to the LabTools people. See the schedule for when
					you have to do this.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>
		</DropdownGroup>

		<DropdownGroup title="Application">
			<Dropdown title="Do I need to have a team?">
				<p>
					No. You are more than welcome to make a team before the hackathon, but loads of people come without
					a team. We will help everyone find a team Friday night. We allow groups of 3-5 persons, but
					recommend groups of 4.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="How can I apply?">
				<p>Sign-ups for this year's AUHack have closed.</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="Can I attend?">
				<p>
					You might think that a hackathon is for programmers only, but that's not true. Technology and code
					is one thing - creative minds, bright insights and strategic eyes are another. So, as long as you
					are a student above 18 years old, you are more than welcome. Actually, we believe that the more
					different people we are, the better.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>
		</DropdownGroup>

		<DropdownGroup title="Logistics">
			<Dropdown title="What do I need to bring?">
				<p>
					A laptop, cellphone and chargers, as well as a well-rested mind. If you want to hack on hardware,
					you might need to bring it yourself. What you won't need to bring is a pre-determined team, an idea
					for a hack, nor food and drinks. Also, there is absolutely no reason to bring a bad mood.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="When is it?">
				<p>
					AUHack will start in the evening of Friday and end Sunday. All work eligible for prizes must be
					worked on and completed during this period of time and can't be prepared from home.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="Can I sleep at the AUHack venue?">
				<p>Currently, we will not be offering the opportunity to sleep at AUHack 2026.</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="How do I get there?">
				<p>
					The address is: <a href="https://goo.gl/maps/UMjBPRkJ5u62" target="_blank"
						>Finlandsgade 21, 8200 Aarhus N</a
					>
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="Will there be parking available?">
				<p>
					The streets around the venue should provide suitable parking for all participants. Additionally
					there is a parking lot near the venue.
				</p>
			</Dropdown>
		</DropdownGroup>
		<DropdownGroup title="Help!">
			<Dropdown title="What if this FAQ didn't answer my questions?">
				<p>
					Send an email to: <a href="mailto:contact@auhack.dk">contact@auhack.dk</a>
				</p>
			</Dropdown>

			<Dropdown title="I don't want to hack, I want to _______!">
				<p>
					If you'd like to be a part of AUHack but don't want to hack, we also need spirited volunteers to
					help bring the event to life. Shoot us an e-mail at: <a href="mailto:contact@auhack.dk"
						>contact@auhack.dk</a
					>
				</p>
			</Dropdown>
		</DropdownGroup>
	</Section>
</BaseLayout>
